answers:
1. The positive integer $n$ that satisfies the given equation is 2. So the correct answer is "None of these".

2. We have the equation
\[\arctan\frac {1}{3} + \arctan\frac {1}{4} + \arctan\frac {1}{5} + \arctan\frac {1}{n} = \frac {\pi}{4}.\]
Let $A = \arctan\frac{1}{3}$ and $B = \arctan\frac{1}{4}$. Then
\begin{align*} \tan(A+B) &= \frac{\tan A + \tan B}{1-\tan A \tan B} \\ &= \frac{\frac{1}{3}+\frac{1}{4}}{1-\frac{1}{3}\cdot\frac{1}{4}} \\ &= \frac{\frac{7}{12}}{1-\frac{1}{12}} = \frac{\frac{7}{12}}{\frac{11}{12}} = \frac{7}{11}\end{align*} 
Let $C = \arctan\frac{1}{5}$. Then
\begin{align*} \tan((A+B)+C) &= \frac{\tan(A+B)+\tan C}{1-\tan(A+B)\tan C} \\ &= \frac{\frac{7}{11}+\frac{1}{5}}{1-\frac{7}{11}\cdot\frac{1}{5}} \\ &= \frac{\frac{35+11}{55}}{1-\frac{7}{55}} = \frac{\frac{46}{55}}{\frac{48}{55}} = \frac{46}{48} = \frac{23}{24}\end{align*} 
Then
\begin{align*}\arctan\frac{1}{3}+\arctan\frac{1}{4}+\arctan\frac{1}{5}+\arctan\frac{1}{n} &= \frac{\pi}{4} \\ \arctan\frac{23}{24}+\arctan\frac{1}{n} &= \frac{\pi}{4} \\ \tan\left(\arctan\frac{23}{24} + \arctan\frac{1}{n}\right) &= \tan\frac{\pi}{4} = 1 \\ \frac{\frac{23}{24}+\frac{1}{n}}{1-\frac{23}{24}\cdot\frac{1}{n}} &= 1 \\ \frac{23}{24}+\frac{1}{n} &= 1-\frac{23}{24n} \\ \frac{23n+24}{24n} &= \frac{24n-23}{24n} \\ 23n+24 &= 24n-23 \\ n &= 47\end{align*} 

3. E

